# This repository holds one page and its furniture, not a build. A stock
# language template was deliberately not carried in, on the principle that an
# ignore file full of rules that cannot fire teaches the next reader to skim
# it. Everything below is here because the incident it prevents is possible.

# Environment and key material. Nothing here needs credentials, which is
# exactly when this is cheap to add: a key committed once is compromised even
# after the file is deleted, so the rule has to predate the key rather than
# follow it. This repository is public, which makes the point sharper.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa
id_ed25519
keys.txt

# Local agent configuration. Deliberately untracked: settings files here
# accumulate machine-specific absolute paths and permission allowlists, which
# are a property of one workstation rather than of this project.
.claude/

# Python byte cache. `scripts/` holds the vendored checks, and running them
# locally writes this. A `.pyc` reached a sibling repository's index the same
# day its `scripts/` directory was added, so this is a rule rather than a
# claim that it cannot happen.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
